{"name":"Tahini","hex":"#ddbb77","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tahini","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paste made from ground sesame seeds, and used to make hummus, baba ganoush, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tahini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tahini","blocks":[{"text":"Tahini is a Middle Eastern condiment made from ground sesame seeds. The most common variety comes from hulled seeds, but unhulled ones can also be used; the latter variety is slightly bitter, but more nutritious. The seeds are more commonly roasted than raw. Tahini can be served by itself, made into a salad dressing, or used as a major ingredient in hummus, baba ghanoush, or halva."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Tahina.JPG/330px-Tahina.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahini","wikidata":"Q383389"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG/500px-Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG/1280px-Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG/500px-Tahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tahini made with roasted sesame, dubbed \"red tahini\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATahini_with_roasted_sesame.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Black_sesame_paste.jpg/500px-Black_sesame_paste.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Black_sesame_paste.jpg/1280px-B